{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1372393-alternate-data-sphere","id":1372393,"title":"Alternate Data Sphere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-03T00:33:17-08:00","id":1372393,"title":"Alternate Data Sphere","content":"So: the Data Sphere we got in NWO and M20 is basically a reskinning of Correspondence with a technological veneer. That's nice and all; but it's not quite what I imagine when I think of a Data Sphere. This thread is intended to correct that. In addition, it involves a few house rules that I apply to matters pertaining to the Digital Web \u2014 something else that I like in theory, but am not nearly as find of in implementation. <br /> <br /> Let's start with Web Access (Digital Web Systems, M20 pp.466\u2013473). <br /> <br /> <i>Sensory Visitation</i> isn't something that anyone can do; it always requires an Effect to access the Digital Web. In particular, regular VR gear lets you access mundane VR simulations; but it doesn't let you access the Digital Web which exists one layer \u201cdeeper\u201d. To engage in Sensory Visitation, you need one dot in Correspondence or Data. To the extent that a Sleeper can access the Digital Web, it's because the VR gear that he's using is a one-dot Wonder that contains a Coincidental \u201cSensory Visitation\u201d Effect. <br /> <br /> For the traditional VA Focus, the most common Instrument for this Effect would be VR gear; and given that most mages who mess with the Digital Web tend to be technomancers, they tend to share the same Instruments that the VAs pioneered. Not all of them do, though; and mages can eventually dispense with their Instruments, accessing the Digital Web without any gear. <br /> <br /> Sensory Visitation is also more about AR (\u201cAugmented Reality\u201d) than about VR (\u201cVirtual Reality\u201d): it lets you look at your surroundings and see virtual displays hovering over things providing relevant information that can be found about it in the Digital Web. In game terms, this \u201cAugmented Reality\u201d tends to play out as Magick Enhancing Abilities, mostly as applied to the Computer Systems rules found in <b>Book of Secrets</b> (pp.116\u2013127). <br /> <br /> Astral Immersion still requires two dots of Correspondence or Data; but as with Sensory Visitation, the business about VR gear is actually a matter of your Focus Instruments, not a hardwired requirement. You don't even need the Intelligence+Computer roll; that's merely an application of Abilities Enhancing Magick. <br /> <br /> Holistic Immersion is \u201cmerely\u201d a minor variation of <i>Transform a Body into an Element</i> (M20 p.508), where the \u201celement\u201d is data and with the added effect that your now-Virtual body gets transferred into the Digital Web: so Life 3/Data 3 or Life 4/Data 3. Again, any hardware requirements are a matter of one's choice of Instruments. <br /> <br /> More generally, Data treats digital information as a \u201csubstance\u201d in much the same way that Spirit treats ephemera: it's a Pattern; just not a physical Pattern. In fact, Data interacts with memophores (M20 pp.638\u2013639) in the same way that Spirit interacts with spirits. It may even be possible to treat Holistic Immersion as a sort of \u201cStepping Sideways\u201d into the Digital Web, letting you do it with just Data. In short, there are a lot of parallels between Data and Spirit. <br /> <br /> Another change from existing rules is that Data doesn't require the destination to be connected to the Internet, per se; that's \u201cmerely\u201d the use of the Internet as an Instrument. And as with the ability to Surpass your Instruments to access the Digital Web without VR gear, it's also possible to Surpass your Instruments to connect to a location that isn't connected to the internet. <br /> <br /> And what is perhaps the biggest difference between Correspondence and Data is that Data drops all of the space-warping capabilities such as teleportation, co-locality, and spatial mutation, keeping only the Correspondence Sphere Ranges (or rather, the Data Connections) and the Digital Web access described above, and replaces the rest with an assortment of Effects adapted primarily from the Mind Sphere, but with concepts such as \u201cthought\u201d reframed as \u201cdata processes\u201d and \u201cmemory\u201d reframed as \u201cdata storage\u201d. Illusion effects become sensor spoofing, telepathy becomes digital interface (with some substantial shifts to bring it in line with the implications of Digital Web access), and so on. As per <b>Book of Secrets</b> p.154, Data can also be used to help craft software Wonders. <br /> <br /> So basically, Data is a blend of limited variants of Correspondence, Mind, and Spirit. <br /> <br /> Does this strike people as useful? Does it pass the Goldilocks test (not too much, not too little)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}